Ringsmith ER-035 (ruling LuciDin 19 Nov 2026, docs/decomp_recipes.md 3.5)

ee-as for the r5900: no coprocessor-move hazard nop between mtc1 (or another INSN_COPROC_MOVE_DELAY
instruction) and the next instruction that uses its register, when assembled in reorder mode. In .set
noreorder blocks nothing changes. The game has 1,454 such sites (SDK 19) with the use directly after the
move and none with a nop between. Same form as ee-as_r5900_fpcc_reorder.patch; a documented
reconstruction of Sony's assembler behaviour, not Sony's code.

Applies to SSXModding/ps2-ee-toolchain b595ded, directory ee/ (patch -p1 -d <src>/ee), with or without
ee-as_r5900_fpcc_reorder.patch.

--- a/gas/config/tc-mips.c
+++ b/gas/config/tc-mips.c
@@ -1452,7 +1452,8 @@
       else if (! mips_opts.mips16
 	       && mips_opts.isa < 4
 	       && (((prev_pinfo & INSN_COPROC_MOVE_DELAY)
-                    && ! cop_interlocks)
+                    && ! cop_interlocks
+		    && ! (mips_cpu == 5900 && ! mips_opts.noreorder)) /* Ringsmith ER-035 */
 		   || (mips_opts.isa < 2
 		       && (prev_pinfo & INSN_COPROC_MEMORY_DELAY))))
 	{
